[38.069978, "o", "python3 -c \"from bytewax.operators import DynamicSink, StatelessSinkPartition; help(StatelessSinkPartition)\" 2>&1 | head -50\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[38.168308, "o", "Help on class StatelessSinkPartition in module bytewax.outputs:\r\n\r\nclass StatelessSinkPartition(abc.ABC, typing.Generic)\r\n |  Output partition that is stateless.\r\n |\r\n |  Method resolution order:\r\n |      StatelessSinkPartition\r\n |      abc.ABC\r\n |      typing.Generic\r\n |      builtins.object\r\n |\r\n |  Methods defined here:\r\n |\r\n |  close(self) -> None\r\n |      Cleanup this partition when the dataflow completes.\r\n |\r\n |      This is not guaranteed to be called. It will only be called\r\n |      when the dataflow finishes on finite input. It will not be\r\n |      called during an abrupt or abort shutdown.\r\n |\r\n |  write_batch(self, items: List[~X]) -> None\r\n |      Write a batch of output items.\r\n |\r\n |      Called multiple times whenever new items are seen at this\r\n |      point in the dataflow.\r\n |\r\n |      :arg items: Items in the dataflow. Non-deterministically\r\n |          batched.\r\n |\r\n |  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n |  Data descriptors defined here:\r\n |\r\n |  __dict__\r\n |      dictionary for instance variables\r\n |\r\n |  __weakref__\r\n |      list of weak references to the object\r\n |\r\n |  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n |  Data and other attributes defined here:\r\n |\r\n |  __abstractmethods__ = frozenset({'write_batch'})\r\n |\r\n |  __annotations__ = {}\r\n |\r\n |  __orig_bases__ = (<class 'abc.ABC'>, typing.Generic[~X])\r\n |\r\n |  __parameters__ = (~X,)\r\n |\r\n |  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n"]
